{title: A New Commandment}
{subtitle: John 13:34–35}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] |
| [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The [Bb]supper on the table and the [Dm7]lamps were burning low
He [Ebmaj7]knelt down with a basin, it was [F7sus4]time for him to go
He [Bb]washed the dust from every foot, the doubter [Dm7]and the proud
And then [Gm7]he spoke [Cm7]so gently, though his heart was cry[F7sus4]ing loud
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
A new commandment [Bb]I give you: love one another
[Dm7]As I have loved you, [Eb]so you must love one another
[F7sus4]By this everyone will know that [Bb]you are my disciples
If [Dm7]you have love for one [Gm7]an[Cm7]other
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Not [F7sus4]just the easy neigh[Bb]bors, not just the ones we choose
[Dm7]Not just when love is sim[Ebmaj7]ple and there's nothing much to lose
[F7sus4]The towel and the basin, the bread [Bb]passed hand to hand
This [Dm7]is the way he [Gm7]loved [Cm7]us, this is his command
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F7sus4]A new commandment [Bb]I give you: love one another
[Dm7]As I have loved you, [Eb]so you must love one anoth[F7sus4]er
By this everyone will know [Bb]that you are my disciples
If [Dm7]you have love for one [Gm7]anoth[Cm7]er
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Love one anoth[F7sus4]er
As I have loved [Bb]you
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
